<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    VENDORED COPY of VirtualBox 7.2.6's own
    /usr/share/virtualbox/UnattendedTemplates/win_nt6_unattended.xml, with ONE
    additive change: four new RunAsynchronousCommand entries (Order 6-9) in
    the "specialize" pass's existing Microsoft-Windows-Deployment
    RunAsynchronous block, disabling Windows Update-related services BEFORE
    OOBE/FirstLogonCommands run (see below). Diff against upstream before
    passing the script-template option with a newer/older VirtualBox version;
    this file is not kept in sync automatically.

    WHY: confirmed live 2026-11-02 that a Windows-Update-triggered restart
    (event log reason "Operating System: Upgrade (Planned)") raced this
    pipeline's first-boot window and interrupted VBoxManage's own
    win_postinstall.cmd template BEFORE it ever reached our
    the post-install-command option (Enable-WinRmAutomation.ps1) at all; confirmed
    via C:\vboxpostinstall.log never reaching its "Running custom user
    command" line. Enable-WinRmAutomation.ps1 ALSO disables wuauserv (defense
    in depth), but that runs in the oobeSystem pass's FirstLogonCommands,
    which is LATE: Windows Setup's own NetworkLocation/network bring-up
    happens earlier (oobeSystem, before FirstLogonCommands) and an update was
    evidently already staged (download+commit, independent of wuauserv's
    running state) well before Enable-WinRmAutomation.ps1 got a chance to
    disable it; confirmed live: manually disabling wuauserv on an
    already-stuck VM did NOT stop an already-staged update from applying.
    Disabling the update-related services in the EARLIER specialize pass
    (this file) instead closes most of that timing gap.

    BUG FIXED 2026-11-02: an earlier revision of this file mistakenly placed
    those 4 commands in the windowsPE pass's RunAsynchronous block instead of
    the specialize pass's own block (both passes happen to have a same-named
    Microsoft-Windows-Deployment component with its own RunAsynchronous list,
    which is easy to conflate when editing). wuauserv/UsoSvc are not real
    services inside WinPE, so sc.exe failed there and Windows Setup itself
    aborted with "Windows installation encountered an unexpected error. Error
    code: 0x80070002 - 0x40030", confirmed live via VBoxManage screenshotpng
    against a stuck VM. The 4 commands now live ONLY in the specialize pass's
    block (Order 6-9, after its own pre-existing Order 1-5); don't move them
    back to the windowsPE pass.

    Original VirtualBox copyright notice follows unmodified below.
-->
